downlink-frame-queue

Hands frames from a downlink dump to worker processes. Dispatch is one Perl script, workers are
small C binaries, the glue is sh. Nothing here knows what the frames contain.

  ./bin/dispatch.pl -q queue/ -w 4 -c ./worker

The dispatcher reads queue/, hands each frame to a free worker over a pipe, collects exit codes and
writes queue/done/<id> or queue/fail/<id> with the reason. A frame that fails twice goes to
queue/dead/ and is not retried.

Frame ids are the dump offset in hex. Order does not matter, workers are independent.

Layout

  bin/dispatch.pl   queue walker, worker pool, retry bookkeeping
  src/worker.c      worker, reads one frame from stdin
  scripts/requeue.sh  move a dead frame back to the queue
  doc/queue.txt     directory layout and exit codes
  tests/            three frames and the expected classification
- usage
